# DTF tier manifest: ledger-triggers-authoritative  (issue #2992)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The whole gate is local: format-handler
# uploads plus direct catalog-table mutations, checked against the
# repository_usage_ledger counters in Postgres.
#
# The #2992 class: `repository_usage_ledger` (migration 171) was maintained by
# almost none of the write paths — ~90 `INSERT INTO artifacts` sites in the
# format handlers, the proxy-cache catalog writers and ~21 `oci_blobs` writers
# (plus ~30 scattered soft/hard delete sites) mutate the source tables without
# touching the ledger, so the stored counters drift until the background
# reconciler happens to run. Anything that trusts those counters (the planned
# O(1) quota admission repoint) then over-admits against stale bytes, and a
# decrement of never-charged bytes floors below reality (phantom free quota).
#
# The fix (migration 183): row-level AFTER triggers on `artifacts`,
# `proxy_cache_artifacts` and `oci_blobs` charge/decrement the matching ledger
# component inside the mutating statement's own transaction, for every present
# and future write path, with a one-time true-up backfill.
#
# Oracle (discriminating): the invariant "ledger == authoritative live SUM
# after every mutation".
#   * upload a Maven jar through the format handler (a path that never calls
#     the enforced admission code) -> hosted_bytes must equal the live
#     filtered SUM (> 0). Pre-183: ledger row absent/zero            -> FAIL.
#   * raw INSERT / soft-delete / hard DELETE on `artifacts` -> ledger tracks
#     each step exactly and never goes below reality/negative.
#   * raw INSERT into `proxy_cache_artifacts` / `oci_blobs` -> each charges
#     its own component.
#   Fixed (183): every check holds                                    -> PASS.
#
# NOTE: the pre-fix backend image is EXPECTED TO FAIL this oracle (stale
# ledger after the handler upload). That failing run is the proof the oracle
# discriminates; it flips to PASS on the #2992 trigger migration.
#
# Regression leg: quota admission behaviour is UNCHANGED by #2992 (main keeps
# its live-SUM admission): an under-quota enforced upload is 201 and an
# over-quota one is 507 on both images.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + repo creates +
# several uploads back-to-back through one admin.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
